    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18">
        <head>VI Atr Lat 18</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-k">Pecunia quoque Romana erga beatorum sollempnitatem apostolorum Petri et Pauli pontificibus' per singulos annos reddatur.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="51"><ref target="clause:VAtr_11-1">V Atr 11.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin paraphrase of VI Atr (early 11th c.; K = Cotton Claudius A III f. 30, perhaps by Archbishop Wulfstan). Liebermann gives no German translation for it: for the meaning see the matching Old English chapter of VI Atr above, which it paraphrases (Liebermann prints in small type the words that correspond exactly to the Old English).</note>
      </div>
